### The Difference

The main difference is that SELECT ANY TABLE allows the user to use SELECT ... FOR UPDATE, which can acquire row locks and potentially cause blocking.

READ ANY TABLE is intended for read-only access and does not allow SELECT ... FOR UPDATE.

|                               | `SELECT ANY TABLE` | `READ ANY TABLE` |
| ----------------------------- | ------------------ | ---------------- |
| **Available since**           | Older versions     | 12c (12.1.0.2+) |
| **Plain `SELECT`**            | ✅                | ✅              |
| **`SELECT ... FOR UPDATE`**   | ✅                | ❌              |
| **`LOCK TABLE`**              | ✅                | ❌              |
| **Can block other sessions?** | **Yes**           | **No**           |
| **Truly read-only?**          | ❌               | ✅               |



